-- title:
--   Unipotent-fixed vector gives a map to a principal series
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive natural number and let $g$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity at coprime arguments, and the two recursions at prime powers according as the prime divides $M$ or not) and for no proper divisor $M'\mid M$ does the eigensystem of $g$ away from $M$ occur in a normalised eigenform of level $M'$. Let $q$ be a prime, and let $\Phi$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb{Q}$ which is an adelic lift of $g$: it is left invariant under the global points $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, right invariant under the finite level-one subgroup attached to the ideal $(M)$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, and at every adelic matrix with trivial finite part and archimedean component of positive determinant its value is the weight-$2$ slash of $g$ by that archimedean component, evaluated at $i$. Write $\mathcal{W}=$ [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) $\Phi$ for the complex span of the adelic translates $h\cdot\Phi$, with its action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$. Let $y$ be a vector of $\mathcal{W}$ fixed by the congruence subgroup [`FLT.SmoothVectors.gl2CongruenceSubgroup q 1`](def/RepTheory_GL2CongruenceSubgroup.html#L181), consisting of those $h\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ all of whose entries of $h-1$ and of $h^{-1}-1$ have norm at most $q^{-1}$; assume $y\neq 0$ and that $y$ is fixed, under the representation [`LocalNewvector.gl2ReductionRep`](def/LocalNewvector_ReductionFunctor.html#L187) of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ on these fixed vectors obtained by descending the action along `gl2ReductionHom`, by every upper unipotent matrix $\begin{pmatrix}1&t\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ with $t\in\mathbb{Z}/q$. Then there exist monoid homomorphisms $\mu_1,\mu_2:\mathbb{Q}_q^{\times}\to\mathbb{C}^{\times}$ and a nonzero $\mathbb{C}$-linear map $f$ from $\mathcal{W}$ to the carrier [`LocalNewvector.PSCarrier q μ₁ μ₂`](def/LocalNewvector_PrincipalSeriesCarrier.html#L173) of the principal series attached to $\mu_1,\mu_2$ such that $f(x\cdot v)=x\cdot f(v)$ for all $x\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ and all $v$.
--
--   This is the step which, from a nonzero vector of the local representation at $q$ generated by an adelic lift of a newform that is fixed by the principal congruence subgroup of level $q$ and by the upper unipotent subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_q)$, produces a nonzero intertwiner into a principal series, so that the local component at $q$ is not supercuspidal. It is used in contrapositive form by [`CuspForm.IsNewform.gl2ReductionRep_unipotent_fixed_eq_zero_of_forall_linearMap_psCarrier_eq_zero`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.gl2ReductionRep_unipotent_fixed_eq_zero_of_forall_linearMap_psCarrier_eq_zero), which concludes that such unipotent-fixed vectors vanish when no nonzero equivariant map into any principal series exists.
